back in the days of Battlefield Bad  Company a new mode was launched in the  series that gave it a fresh taste both  for vets and casuals of the series that  mode was called rush where you and your  team either destroyed or defended a  series of crates in a fixed location  from your enemies now new on the horizon  is battlefield one which is hoping this  new mode will recapture that excitement  the same way rush did picture if you  will rush and conquest having a baby  that little bastard would be named  operations the setup for this mode may  sound familiar for veterans of the  series a large map consisting of five to  seven battle sections with two or three  captured flags in each the object of  this mode is to capture and hold flags  while the defending team must hold the  line until the ticket count runs out at  any time similar to conquest the  defending team can retake a captured  flag while the game is still fixed in  that battle location if the attacking  team captures all Flags the defenders  will be given a few seconds to either  retake a flag or fall back and put a  better defenses at the next section one  match consists of three rounds  more so in favor to the attacking team  in the last two rounds when the  attacking team is held in a battle  section by the defending team after  round 1 round 2 kicks off with the  summoning of the behemoth for the  attacking team this behemoth as seen in  other modes can either be a battleship  armored train or a Zeppelin each packing  enough firepower to aid the attacking  team to push forward to the defenders  main base at the end of each map  the addition of a behemoth to the  attacking team only is a nice add-on  since through my experience the majority  of the maps favorite bit to the  defenders cup of tea also to add to the  fact is that if the defending team  manages to destroy the behemoth and  round two and hold the enemy either in  the same or new battle section the third  and final round sees the attacking team  getting back a brand new behemoth which  feels a bit unfair given the fact that  most of the rounds I played saw the  first behemoth pushed my team to our  second-to-last base by the end of round  two adding one at the start of round 3  we either find enjoyment by the  community or a mode breaking add-on that  many might want changed right away so  what really makes this better than Rush  well to be honest with you rush was a  great example back when it first  launched on bad company all the way to  where it is today of really tight team  coordinator  tax operations take this a whole nother  step further bigger and wider range of  maps to be used now you don't worry  about planning objectives on crates that  you have to defend or worry about  enemies camping now you can just capture  flags you can stay within their  parameters so you don't to worry about  having to sit around and wait for an  enemy to sneak up behind you you can  kind of planned your attacks to how you  see fit the mode just feels like a  breath of fresh air that many of us who  in plane battlefield for so many years  have really been asking for for quite a  while  in my nine hours of early play no mode  gave me more intense battles than  operations with 64 players running  around in lag free maps like the urban  chaos of arms the deadly Mountain Alps  of Montegrappa  and the blood-stained countryside of San  Quentin's car just to name a few this  mode is set to mix it up in battlefield  multi players world the same as rushed  it back in the start of bad company with  this and so much being thrown into  battlefield one it's shaping up to  possibly be one of the best bow fields  to come out in years what are you  looking forward to doing in operations  do you feel it's fair or unfair for the  attacking team to get a second chance of  controlling a behemoth feel free to  share your thoughts below in the  comments and we will see you guys on the  battlefield  for more on your favorite games keep it  here on GameSpot for more
 

